<p class="sst-lead">Treat the CLO as an integral kernel. Its eigenfunctions are a second-kind, homogeneous
Fredholm integral equation,</p>

<p>\[ (\mathcal{K}_{\mathcal{T}}\,v)[\bm{c}](s) = \sigma^2\, v(s). \]</p>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p>In words:</p>
  <blockquote>Encode all pairwise angles (<em>rigid invariance</em>) between <em>centered landmarks</em> generated
  by the curve, <em>separated from scale</em>.</blockquote>
</div>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p>Equivalently, in the inner-product form over the Hilbert space \(\mathcal{H}_d\),</p>
  <p>\[ \langle k_{\mathcal{T}}[\bm{c}](s,\cdot),\, v\rangle_{\mathcal{H}_d} = \sigma^2\, v(s). \]</p>
</div>
